>
> What are the keys to success in NetHack?

The primary one is to learn two lessons from every death.

Lesson one is tactics.  What killed you is something specific.
Learn about that type of death and puzzle over how to handle
it the next time.

Lesson two is strategy.  Very many deaths are not the result
of a something you did in the last 10 moves but a result of a
decision you made at least 2 levels ago.

Of the two lessons, the strategy one is much more important
in the long run and much more difficult to figure out: You died
in a crowd?  Learning to slow your exploration is more important
than learning to kill a specific type of monster.

Lesson two is learning use of resources.  It is very easy to
not spend resources to save them for later (wands, scrolls,
potions when in combat because regular ascenders discuss
saving them) and spending resources without knowing their
limits (melee weapons to expert is almost always a trap in
the early game).  The DevTeam put very many features into
the game that are temptation traps.

